{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NpeN52K9pyCaDDq9Y4zCRk","type":"tool_result","content":"18\n15\n## Bugfixes\n- Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir).\n- Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.\n- Also apply the path-separator diagnostic to `--and` patterns, which are matched against the file name just like the primary pattern.\n- Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4d5b15d-f1c4-4f0f-8505-da71980ba186","uuid":"46cb5695-07f7-415d-a684-57994e6a4cad","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:49:20.410Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"18\n15\n## Bugfixes\n- Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir).\n- Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.\n- Also apply the path-separator diagnostic to `--and` patterns, which are matched against the file name just like the primary pattern.\n- Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/tmp/tlw-33obvus2/CHANGELOG.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":6,"newStart":7,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Bugfixes"," - Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir)."," - Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.","+- Also apply the path-separator diagnostic to `--and` patterns, which are matched against the file name just like the primary pattern."," - Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty)."," "," # 10.4.2"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/tmp/tlw-33obvus2/CHANGELOG.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NpeN52K9pyCaDDq9Y4zCRk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
